    {
      "id": "SAA-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-stickelberger-carry-classes",
      "title": "Carries annihilate ideal classes in a cyclotomic field",
      "statement": "For any ideal class x and residues a,b modulo M, the product of the inverse Galois translates of x at residues with a carry is the trivial ideal class. Summing the carries shows that the floor operator F_h kills x for every h≥0. In particular θ(1−J) kills the entire ideal class group.",
      "hypotheses": "An ideal class in the full cyclotomic field. Choose a prime of rational prime norm outside M to represent it. The Jacobi sum divisibility and carry test apply when a,b,a+b are nonzero. The remaining cases are computed directly.",
      "correspondence": "The exposition recovers the smoothed element directly from a translated floor operator and the sum of all translates. The source first proves a general integral coefficient criterion and specializes it to the same element.",
      "dependencies": [
        "SAA-01",
        "JAC-01",
        "CRL-01",
        "CRL-02"
      ],
